1775	     * The abrupt path of a group of forked arms, whose code starts at
1776	     * groupStart and ends here.  A group completes only when each of its
1777	     * threads has (Specification/basic/evaluation/parallelism.tex, section
1778	     * "Threads and Parallelism"): where arm 0 or a join throws, the handler
1779	     * waits for every arm that was forked, and then throws that exception on.
1780	     * The joins run in the arms' order and each throws what its arm threw,
1781	     * so the exception caught is that of the first arm, in that order, that
1782	     * threw.  An arm that was never forked is not run.  The task locals stay
1783	     * live until the handler has read them.  The table entry is written after
1784	     * the code that it covers, so that a handler inside an arm comes first.
1785	     */
